<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.8"/>
    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Pain and difficulty chewing and speaking with loose, worn complete dentures that click and move; cause and treatment under evaluation with prosthodontics: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Two shallow ulcers under the lower denture flange, probably traumatic from an ill-fitting denture, with no induration, red or white patch, or neck lymph node; to be re-examined two weeks after the denture is left out between meals: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Unintended weight loss of about 5.6 kg (6%) over six months from a narrowed, soft diet; at risk of malnutrition (MNA-SF 10): active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Oral examination and oral cancer screening at every visit: lips, cheeks, tongue, floor of mouth, palate, ridges and neck nodes; a mouth ulcer under a denture is re-examined two weeks after the denture is relieved or left out, and biopsied if it has not healed. Guideline: Evidence-based clinical practice guideline for the evaluation of potentially malignant disorders in the oral cavity: A report of the American Dental Association (2017) [S]</item><item>Prosthodontics consultation to diagnose the edentulous jaws and denture problems, review the ulcers, and plan new dentures and implant options. Guideline: Classification system for complete edentulism. The American College of Prosthodontics (1999); Evidence-based guidelines for the care and maintenance of complete dentures: a publication of the American College of Prosthodontists (2011); The McGill consensus statement on overdentures. Mandibular two-implant overdentures as first choice standard of care for edentulous patients (2002) [S]</item><item>Comfort until the consultation: lower denture out except at meals, a soft diet that still includes protein, acetaminophen as needed, warm salt-water rinses, no denture adhesive on the ulcers. Guideline: Evidence-based guidelines for the care and maintenance of complete dentures: a publication of the American College of Prosthodontists (2011); Evidence-based clinical practice guideline for the evaluation of potentially malignant disorders in the oral cavity: A report of the American Dental Association (2017) [S]</item><item>Nutrition and weight: MNA-SF at intake and on review, weight at every visit, a high-protein soft diet with an oral nutritional supplement twice a day until chewing is restored, and a check of blood count, metabolic panel, albumin, hemoglobin A1c, TSH and vitamin B12 for other causes of weight loss. Guideline: Validation of the Mini Nutritional Assessment short-form (MNA-SF): a practical tool for identification of nutritional status (2009) [S]</item><item>Denture care: clean the dentures daily with a soft brush and a non-abrasive cleanser, keep them out overnight in water, clean the ridges and tongue, and see the prosthodontist each year. Guideline: Evidence-based guidelines for the care and maintenance of complete dentures: a publication of the American College of Prosthodontists (2011) [S]</item><item>Cardiovascular risk: blood pressure, lipids and diabetes screening at the preventive visit; tooth loss is recorded as associated with cardiovascular disease, not as a proven cause, and does not change his risk estimate. Guideline: Periodontal disease and atherosclerotic vascular disease: does the evidence support an independent association? A scientific statement from the American Heart Association (2012); Tooth loss and risk of cardiovascular disease and stroke: A dose-response meta analysis of prospective cohort studies (2018) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
